The rule as written for `_grounding_kernel` says the verdict is given "with no relaxation and the value-in-span check on". No relaxation means the span must occur verbatim in the document. Changing the document from `"hello world"` to `"hello  world"` (two spaces) makes the span `"hello world"` no longer occur verbatim, so the verdict ought to move from GROUNDED to SPAN_NOT_IN_DOCUMENT.